89
00:03:49.229 --> 00:03:50.563
So this is just a little

90
00:03:50.563 --> 00:03:52.131
quirk but the way the interface works.

91
00:03:52.432 --> 00:03:54.434
But we're going to end up being saying true here.

92
00:03:54.634 --> 00:03:56.135
We will define a custom loader that

93
00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:57.837
we're going to add into this part here

94
00:03:57.837 --> 00:04:01.140
for the pdf_loader.
We're going to have a custom splitter as well

95
00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:03.443
because we have some notion of what the markdown looks like.

96
00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:05.712
And if you've done any kind of chunking before,

97
00:04:05.812 --> 00:04:08.414
you know that just doing text splitting itself is an art.

98
00:04:08.615 --> 00:04:10.116
There's probably multiple courses on deep learning

99
00:04:10.116 --> 00:04:11.818
here that you can take a look at

100
00:04:11.818 --> 00:04:14.020
to actually really dig into that topic.

101
00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:16.823
We're going to do a simplified version making some assumptions

102
00:04:16.823 --> 00:04:18.491
about the data that we have. You can also

103
00:04:18.491 --> 00:04:20.326
pass in a schema, and the schema is of course

