00:08:48.027 --> 00:08:49.929
been using for just sending queries to Neo4J.

217
00:08:50.129 --> 00:08:52.398
That singleton lets you grab the internal driver

218
00:08:52.398 --> 00:08:54.934
that it uses.
So that's what we're doing here.

219
00:08:55.201 --> 00:08:57.303
Okay. You've defined some of the utility

220
00:08:57.303 --> 00:08:59.405
functions needed for the knowledge graph pipeline

221
00:08:59.405 --> 00:09:01.274
and also some of the other components

222
00:09:01.274 --> 00:09:03.409
like the LLM and the embedder as well.

223
00:09:03.709 --> 00:09:06.012
And now we're going to turn to the context required

224
00:09:06.012 --> 00:09:08.714
for actually doing the knowledge graph entity extraction.

225
00:09:08.981 --> 00:09:10.983
And we're going to start with the entity schema.

226
00:09:11.384 --> 00:09:14.153
So the entity schema required
by the neo4j_graphrag package

227
00:09:14.153 --> 00:09:16.155
has a couple different components.

228
00:09:16.455 --> 00:09:18.257
One is it wants to know the node types

229
00:09:18.257 --> 00:09:20.159
