00:15:02.935 --> 00:15:05.004
And then also the subject graph,

379
00:15:05.037 --> 00:15:07.306
that's going to have all the extracted entities

380
00:15:07.339 --> 00:15:09.308
and also how they're related to each other.

381
00:15:10.109 --> 00:15:12.912
Now that we have all files processed,

382
00:15:12.912 --> 00:15:16.882
this has been completed.
You now have a lexical graph,

383
00:15:17.116 --> 00:15:19.585
a subject graph, and a domain graph.

384
00:15:19.885 --> 00:15:21.887
However, the knowledge graph isn't complete

385
00:15:22.588 --> 00:15:25.891
because the subject graph
and the domain graph are not connected.

386
00:15:26.392 --> 00:15:28.093
And if you recall, the domain

387
00:15:28.093 --> 00:15:30.095
graph was created from the CSV files.

388
00:15:30.462 --> 00:15:32.665
And we just created the subject graph

389
00:15:32.665 --> 00:15:35.134
as extracting data from markdown files.

390
00:15:35.467 --> 00:15:38.270
The next step is to connect
the entities that we extracted

391
00:15:38.270 --> 00:15:40.973
from the markdown files into the subject graph.

392
00:15:41.373 --> 00:15:44.276
We want to be able to connect those with the domain graph.

393
00:15:44.476 --> 00:15:46.278
So if there are products in the

394
00:15:46.278 --> 00:15:48.347
domain graph that refer to the same product

395
00:15:48.447 --> 00:15:50.950
as the extracted entities in the subject graph,

396
00:15:51.250 --> 00:15:53.152
we want to connect those. So we're going to

397
00:15:53.152 --> 00:15:55.254
define a couple of tools in order to do that.

398
00:15:55.454 --> 00:15:57.756
Now, for each type of entity in the subject

399
00:15:57.756 --> 00:16:00.559
graph, you're going to devise a strategy for correlating

400
00:16:00.559 --> 00:16:02.661
with the right node in the domain graph.

401
00:16:02.962 --> 00:16:05.164
For example, you should expect that the products

402
00:16:05.164 --> 00:16:07.766
with the product names exist in the subject graph.

403
00:16:08.467 --> 00:16:11.470
and that these should correlate
with the products in the domain graph.

404
00:16:11.971 --> 00:16:13.172
So in order to do this,

405
00:16:13.172 --> 00:16:14.573
you will do a couple of things.

406
00:16:15.274 --> 00:16:17.409
First, you're going to find all the

407
00:16:17.409 --> 00:16:19.578
unique entity labels in the subject graph.

408
00:16:20.145 --> 00:16:23.949
Similarly, you'll find all the unique node labels
in the domain graph.

409
00:16:24.650 --> 00:16:26.952
And then you'll attempt to correlate the property keys

410
00:16:26.952 --> 00:16:28.954
between those two different sets of labels.

411
00:16:29.355 --> 00:16:31.156
So you can figure out if there's a product

412
00:16:31.156 --> 00:16:33.959
with a couple of different properties in the subject graph,

413
00:16:34.159 --> 00:16:36.061
how does that correlate with a product

414
00:16:36.061 --> 00:16:37.963
with a couple of different properties in the domain graph.

415
00:16:38.464 --> 00:16:41.266
So that's the very final step is performing entity resolution

416
00:16:41.467 --> 00:16:44.670
by analyzing the similarity of property values.

417
00:16:45.237 --> 00:16:47.039
Okay, the first step is to find

418
00:16:47.039 --> 00:16:49.041
the unique entity labels in the subject graph.

419
00:16:49.341 --> 00:16:51.010
Now, let's take a look at the subject

420
00:16:51.010 --> 00:16:52.644
graph to see what the nodes look like.

