00:19:36.141 --> 00:19:39.444
that's going to look for all nodes
that have that particular label,

492
00:19:39.444 --> 00:19:42.648
but instead, once we've found some sample set of those,

493
00:19:42.648 --> 00:19:45.551
we're going to find just the unique keys
that occur on those.

494
00:19:45.651 --> 00:19:48.153
Let's take a look at what
that utility function looks like.

495
00:19:48.654 --> 00:19:50.789
Here it's going to give an argument which

